@startuml tenant-isolation-current-and-fix
' ============================================================================
'  agentd TENANT ISOLATION - the two live leaks (2026-08) and the ONE-RULE fix.
'  STATUS: FIX BUILT (uncommitted) - pinned by tests/unit/test_tenant_isolation.py.
'  Activity-flowchart view, same conventions as web-agent-request-flow.puml and
'  agent-publish-and-ownership-flow.puml.
'
'  THE TWO LEAKS, one sentence each:
'    #1  _send_all() fans every chat.event to every socket, filtered by AGENT
'        only - user X watches user Y's live run on the same web agent.
'    #2  GET /file serves any absolute path under state_dir - which contains
'        EVERY account's subtree - with no account check at all.
'
'  WHY THE FIX IS NOT "if hosted": the RPC read side never branched and never
'  leaked. It derives every path from ONE fact resolved per connection (the
'  account contextvar), and desktop is simply the case where that fact is the
'  local owner. The leaks are exactly the two egress paths that DON'T consume
'  that fact yet. So the fix is to finish the model, not to add branches:
'
'    every CONNECTION authenticates to a set of IDENTITIES   (ownership.callers)
'    every RUN / FILE has an OWNER                            (stamp_owner)
'    egress = one membership test: owner IN identities        (owned_by_caller)
'
'  Deployment shape changes the VALUES, never the CODE PATH. Desktop local:
'  owner and identities are both "local" -> the test is always true -> today's
'  behaviour byte-for-byte. Hosted: strangers only ever match themselves.
'
'  Render (from this folder):
'    java -jar ../../../plantuml.jar -tpng tenant-isolation-current-and-fix.puml
' ============================================================================

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam ArrowFontColor #444444
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #6A6A6A
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF4E5
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #C9A227
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8DC
skinparam NoteBorderColor #C9B458
skinparam partitionBorderColor #9AA0B5
skinparam partitionFontStyle bold
skinparam partitionFontSize 13

title Tenant isolation - current leaks + the one-rule fix\nONE membership test (owner IN caller identities) at the daemon's two egress choke points\nno `if hosted` anywhere - deployment shape changes the identity VALUES, never the code path

start

partition "0 . THE MODEL - already half-built   (DAEMON, any deployment)" #E8F0FE {
  :**what already works**: every RPC read resolves paths through the
  account contextvar pinned per connection (_handle_conn) - sessions,
  workspace, memory, agent visibility all land in `accounts/<acct>/...`
  and desktop (no account) is the degenerate one-tenant case;
  :**what the leaks have in common**: the two paths that BYPASS the
  contextvar seam - the WebSocket fan-out and the HTTP file server -
  because neither ever learned who a frame or a file BELONGS to;
}

switch (What is leaving the daemon?)

case ( a live chat.event frame )

  partition "1a . BEFORE THE FIX - _broadcast / _send_all   (LEAK #1)" #FDECEA {
    :RunHandle already KNOWS its account_id
    (stamped at _chat_send) - but the outgoing
    frame is never tagged with it;
    :the connection's account exists only as a
    contextvar DURING _handle_conn - it is not
    stored per socket, so the fan-out loop
    could not filter by account even if it tried;
    if (socket is agent-scoped?) then (yes)
      :_scoped_event_allowed: **agent id match ONLY** -
      X and Y both scoped to `agent:bedtime-kids`
      pass each other's filter;
    else (no - host connection)
      :**NO FILTER AT ALL** - an authenticated
      unscoped client receives every account's
      events on the whole daemon;
    endif
    :=> user X watches user Y's run LIVE:
    messages, text deltas, tool results,
    and the absolute PATHS of Y's artifacts;
  }

  partition "1b . THE FIX (BUILT) - identities + one membership test" #E6F4EA {
    :**connection side**: at _handle_conn, store
    `client_identities[ws] = ownership.callers(account, hosted)`
    right where the contextvar is pinned - identity becomes
    CONNECTION state, like client_scopes already is
    (anonymous public sockets hold the EMPTY set);
    :**frame side**: nothing stamped, NO protocol change -
    _send_all derives the frame's owner from the EMISSION
    context (`accounts.account_id()`, else stamp_owner:
    "local" on desktop, "platform" on hosted). Every emitter
    already runs in its actor's context, so every current
    AND future event is scoped automatically;
    :**fan-out**: ONE domain rule - **ownership.may_observe**:
    a deployment-owner identity observes its deployment,
    everyone else strict owner-membership, the unknown
    socket observes nothing (fail closed) - checked for
    EVERY socket (scoped and unscoped alike), THEN the
    existing agent-scope filter applies unchanged;
  }

case ( file bytes via GET /file )

  partition "2a . BEFORE THE FIX - _serve_file   (LEAK #2)" #FDECEA {
    :auth = compare against the FIXED machine bearer only -
    `sess_` tokens are not understood, so on a hosted
    daemon this door is either wide open (no machine
    token configured) or checked against a credential
    web users do not hold;
    :path = an ABSOLUTE path from the query string,
    allowed if under the GLOBAL root list - and
    state_dir is on that list, which contains
    **every** `accounts/<acct>/...` subtree;
    :=> anyone who can reach the port fetches
    Y's workspace files and transcript .jsonl
    by URL - and LEAK #1 hands X those paths;
  }

  partition "2b . THE FIX (BUILT) - same auth rule, caller-shaped roots" #E6F4EA {
    :**authenticate like the socket does**: `_http_identities`
    mirrors the _handle_conn gate exactly - the session
    IDENTIFIES (accounts.resolve, the `?token=` fallback
    every client already sends), the machine token
    authorises only where sign-in is not enforced -
    one rule, two transports, never two doors;
    :**roots follow the caller**: `_file_roots_for(identities)` -
    a deployment owner keeps the legacy whole-world roots,
    an account gets its OWN `accounts/<acct>/...` subtree
    (user_state.account_root - the same resolver every
    write already uses) + the shared read-only
    agent-definition dirs;
    :a cross-account path is then OUTSIDE the caller's
    roots - unreachable by construction, not refused
    by a check someone must remember;
  }

endswitch

partition "3 . WHAT EACH DEPLOYMENT FEELS   (same code, different values)" #E0F2F1 {
  :**desktop LOCAL (signed out)** - identities = {local},
  every run and file owned "local" - the membership test
  is ALWAYS TRUE, roots = the whole home dir:
  today's behaviour byte-for-byte, nothing to configure;
  :**desktop CLOUD MODE (signed in, daemon on the user's PC)** -
  identities = {local, account} (sign-in ADDS, never subtracts) -
  runs owned by either identity still match: single-human
  machine, still sees everything of its own, zero change;
  :**hosted WEB** - identities = {account} - X matches only
  X's runs and X's roots; the operator (machine token) is
  {platform} and sees the deployment's own, a deliberate
  policy VALUE in callers(), not a code branch;
}

partition "4 . WHY EVERY AGENT OBEYS AUTOMATICALLY   (choke points)" #E8F0FE {
  :agents, tools and plugins never see any of this -
  enforcement sits at the daemon's TWO egress doors
  (WS fan-out, HTTP file serving), which every event
  and every byte pass through no matter which agent
  produced them or which surface serves them;
  :same doctrine as agent visibility (_current) and
  publish (withheld_reason): absent one choke point,
  "places that must also check" becomes a list
  somebody forgets to extend;
}

stop

note right
  ==== REUSED, NOT INVENTED ====
  callers() / stamp_owner() / owned_by_caller()
  already exist (domain/ownership.py) and already
  encode desktop-keeps-local, hosted-is-strict.
  The fix teaches the last two egress paths to
  consume the SAME domain rules that agents.list,
  publish and the state resolvers consume today.

  ==== KNOWN RESIDUE, same seam later ====
  * autonomy.sqlite (cron) + auth.sqlite vaults are
    daemon-global - partition like memory_partition
    before offering them hosted
  * no-account runs write the shared layer (by design:
    that layer IS the deployment owner's)
end note

legend left
  | Piece | Today | After the fix |
  | connection identity | contextvar only, lost at fan-out | client_identities[ws] = ownership.callers(...) |
  | event frame | agentId + sessionKey | unchanged - owner derived from the emission context |
  | fan-out filter | _scoped_event_allowed (agent only, scoped sockets only) | ownership.may_observe for ALL sockets, then agent filter |
  | /file auth | fixed machine bearer | _http_identities - the socket gate's own rule |
  | /file roots | global list incl. all of state_dir | _file_roots_for(identities) via user_state.account_root |
  | desktop local | works (single tenant) | identical - membership test degenerates to true |
  | desktop cloud | works (single tenant) | identical - {local, account} both match |
  | hosted web | LEAKS #1 + #2 | X sees only X - by values, not branches |
endlegend

@enduml
